  "rationale": "There are several independent paths to crownData:exfiltrate, so no single blocked step stops the attack. Path A: memoryDump:credentialAccess (reached directly from the vpnGateway or supplychain footholds) leads to jumpHost:lateralMovement, then mailArchive:collection, then the target. jumpHost is also reachable via vpnSession:authenticate, which needs dmzWeb and workstation; both come straight from footholds. Path B: memoryDump plus mailClient:execution give ssoLogin:authenticate, then appServer:lateralMovement, then dbReplica:collection, then the target. Checking each candidate: blocking jumpHost or mailArchive leaves Path B. Blocking ssoLogin, appServer or dbReplica leaves Path A. Blocking memoryDump leaves jumpHost via vpnSession and so mailArchive. Blocking mailClient leaves Path A. Blocking vpnSession, dmzWeb or workstation leaves jumpHost via memoryDump. No other step lies on every path, so there are zero single points of failure."
